  "term": "triazolam",
  "definition": "Triazolam is a triazolobenzodiazepine with sedative-hypnotic effects. It acts at a site on the GABA-A receptor complex on nerve cell membranes, increasing GABA’s inhibitory action and reducing neuronal excitability.",
